urname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of function and usefulness of a pedometer with multi-memory accelerometer</article-title><source>Annual Report of Health Sciences Research Grant on Health Services, Ministry of Health and Welfare, Japan Tokyo</source><year>1999</year><comment>(in Japanese)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McGraw</surname><given-names>KO</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Forming inferences about some intra-class correlation coefficients</article-title><source>Psychol Methods</source><year>1996</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/1082-989X.1.1.30</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bland</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Altman</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Statistical methods for assessing agreement between two methods of clinical measurement</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1986</year><volume>327</volume><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>310</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2868172</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(86)91008-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Atkinson</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Nevill</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comment on the use of concordance correlation to assess the agreement between two variables</article-title><source>Biometrics</source><year>1997</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>775</fpage><lpage>777</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-grou